hemselves teachers after their own lusts,"},{"verse":4,"text":"and will turn away their ears from the truth, and turn away to fables."},{"verse":5,"text":"But you be sober in all things, suffer hardship, do the work of an evangelist, and fulfill your ministry."},{"verse":6,"text":"For I am already being offered, and the time of my departure has come."},{"verse":7,"text":"I have fought the good fight. I have finished the course. I have kept the faith."},{"verse":8,"text":"From now on, the crown of righteousness is stored up for me, which the Lord, the righteous judge, will give to me on that day; and not to me only, but also to all those who have loved his appearing."},{"verse":9,"text":"Be diligent to come to me soon,"},{"verse":10,"text":"for Demas left me, having loved this present world, and went to Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia; and Titus to Dalmatia."},{"verse":11,"text":"Only Luke is with me. Take Mark and bring him with you, for he is useful to me for service."},{"verse":12,"text":"But I sent Tychicus to Ephesus."},{"verse":13,"text":"Bring the cloak that I left at Troas with Carpus when you come—and the books, especially the parchments."},{"verse":14,"text":"Alexander the coppersmith did much evil to me. The Lord will repay him according to his deeds."},{"verse":15,"text":"Beware of him, for he greatly opposed our words."},{"verse":16,"text":"At my first defense, no one came to help me, but all left me. May it not be held against them."},{"verse":17,"text":"But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, that through me the message might be fully proclaimed, and that all the Gentiles might hear. So I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion."},{"verse":18,"text":"And the Lord will deliver me from every evil work and will preserve me for his heavenly Kingdom. To him be the glory forever and ever. Amen."},{"verse":19,"text":"Greet Prisca and Aquila, and the house of Onesiphorus."},{"verse":20,"text":"Erastus remained at Corinth, but I left Trophimus at Miletus sick."},{"verse":21,"text":"Be diligent to come before winter. Eubulus salutes you, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers."},{"verse":22,"text":"The Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Grace be with you. Amen."}],"hasArtwork":true,"artworkUrl":"/data/images/books/2timothy.svg","availableLangs":["zh-CN"]}]